# Per-link escapes for lychee, one entry per line, each with its reason —
# the convention lychee.toml states. lychee runs weekly in scheduled.yml
# over the whole tree; anything listed here would otherwise turn that
# workflow red every Monday for something that is not actually broken.
#
# Nothing goes in here to silence a genuinely dead link.
#
# Entries are REGEXES, not literal URLs — an unanchored entry matches by
# prefix, so every pattern below is escaped and `$`-anchored to match
# exactly one URL.

# The FSF URL in the AGPL-3.0 header line, which appears verbatim in both
# LICENSE and LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt. lychee began scanning it when the
# REUSE layout added the .txt copy (#9) — the extensionless root LICENSE was
# never scanned — and the weekly run went red on the first pass after.
#
# Not rot: the host answers 301 from an ordinary client. It fails only from
# GitHub's hosted runners, with `received fatal alert: HandshakeFailure`,
# which is a TLS negotiation problem between that runner image and fsf.org
# and is not ours to fix at either end.
#
# It cannot be fixed at source either. The licence text is canonical — REUSE
# checks LICENSES/*.txt against the upstream wording, and editing a licence
# to satisfy a link checker is not a thing to do regardless. `$`-anchored,
# so any other fsf.org link — one we actually wrote — would still be caught.
^https://fsf\.org/$
